going to include O_NONBLOCK and a flag.

150
00:08:57,071 --> 00:09:01,900
So we can tell whether or not the user
has requested nonblocking mode.

151
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:06,621
And so the scull handler here for open,

152
00:09:06,621 --> 00:09:12,641
if it sees that the scull
device is not available.

153
00:09:12,641 --> 00:09:15,692
So in this particular
implementation there are some

154
00:09:15,692 --> 00:09:20,220
restrictions that mean that the device
